Case and path spelling set the response strength. Recent programming/genetics
words downweight lowercase library mentions; preceding public/free boosts them.
A byte buffer recognizes split spellings, including Chinese/Japanese library
names. Smaller rules cover literacy/reading words and habit ideographs.
Country-flag letter fragments are negative. Document-initial 12/122 and Title:
are separate responses. Other tokens give zero; history resets per document.
This approximates the main lexical pattern, not the many incidental byte effects.
