"""layers.1.mlp.down_proj:537: a verb-after-subject detector (mostly negative).

The component goes negative on the verb that follows a noun subject. Its
strongest case is a copula after a plain "The/This/... <noun>" subject:
"The product [is]", "The person [is]", "The building [is]" (about -0.7). After
other content words it is weaker ("the value [is]", "many people [are]", about
-0.2). After a pronoun ("it is", "they are", "there is") or punctuation it is
about zero. Reporting and description verbs after a noun subject ("the speaker
[says]", "the sample [shows]") go to -0.5, and modals ("the model [will]") to
-0.2. The first token of each document is slightly positive (+0.09), where the
context resets.

Only the current token and the two before it are read, plus the document
boundary. Everything else is predicted as 0. The rest of the activation (small
values spread over most tokens, and the positive "of" in "the set of") is not
modelled, so only about a tenth of the variance is explained.
