"""A small byte-boundary and document-opening approximation.

A bare UTF-8 continuation byte is interpreted with the preceding bytes. It
usually contributes positively when it finishes an East Asian letter, especially
hiragana or a flag letter, and negatively for combining/control characters.
There is also a negative document-opening response, with a much larger dip for
an opening '12'. Ordinary tokens are mostly left near zero. The much larger responses to
individual Han characters are not reconstructed by these broad classes.
