"""Two responses: Czech/Slovak spelling and opening markup punctuation.

Short tokens beginning with č, š, or ž are positive, especially following
Czech/Slovak diacritics. For isolated consonants, a preceding long vowel
weakens the response. Nine word-initial function-word spellings have their
own contextual values. Context is the last 192 decoded characters, reset
at document boundaries.
